  "description": "The proposal is to extend previously granted single storey rear extension scheme Ref: 192629HH from 3.4m to 4.8m. \n\nThe proposals appearance and scale takes precedent from other extensions in the area to avoid any detrimental impact on the amenities of the neighbouring properties.\n\nThe ground floor rear proposal extends the full width of the house (4.9m) and outwards by 4.8m.  There is a flat roof with an eaves height of 3m (3.2m top of parapet) which aligns with the top of the extension at No.16 Speldhurst Road. The flank walls are brick, to match the existing rear elevation. The walls have no outlook onto neighbouring properties, both of which have rear extensions. A parapet conceals a 0.18m  high rooflight upstand which allows natural light into the centre of the house. The new rear elevation will have glazed bi-fold doors to create a bright living space.",
